cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Variance-aware evaluation of CPC18 choice prediction models: training and analysis code"
abstract: >-
  Training and analysis code of a variance-aware evaluation of behavioral
  choice prediction models on the Choice Prediction Competition 2018 (CPC18).
  It trains four neural and two tree-based models hundreds of times per
  condition from shared seed pools, decouples weight initialization from data
  order in a factorial design, runs two hyperparameter ablations, and repeats
  a subset of conditions on other machines and CPU instruction-set tiers. The
  analysis scripts compute the statistics, tables and figures of the
  accompanying article: fitted lower-tail targets, misranking probabilities by
  Monte Carlo and Bootstrap, variance components and cross-machine agreement.
